    <!--
      Assessment completion screen.

      Three outcomes, three screens. The screen used to say "Report Generated
      Successfully!" no matter what happened, including when the report had not
      been saved at all - so a student whose run did not finish was told it had.
      Wording stays plain: the student did nothing wrong, and none of these
      strings should leak internal vocabulary.
    -->
    <string name="report_state_ok_icon">✅</string>
    <string name="report_state_attention_icon">⚠️</string>

    <!-- Saved, complete. Unchanged from the original success screen. -->
    <string name="report_saved_title">Report Generated Successfully!</string>
    <string name="report_saved_body">Your personalized career report is ready.\nYou can preview it now or continue to home.</string>

    <!-- Saved, but built from general content because generation did not finish.
         This is what a first-time student gets when the run does not complete. -->
    <string name="report_generic_title">Your Report Is Incomplete</string>
    <string name="report_generic_body">We couldn\'t finish building your report, so it contains general guidance instead of feedback on your answers.\nRetake the assessment when you can to get your full personalized report.</string>

    <!-- Not saved: an earlier complete report was kept rather than replaced. -->
    <string name="report_kept_title">This Attempt Didn\'t Finish</string>
    <string name="report_kept_body">We couldn\'t finish building your new report, so your earlier report has been kept and is the one shown.\nYour answers from this attempt weren\'t used. You can take the assessment again.</string>
    <string name="report_preview_button">📄 Preview Report</string>
    <string name="report_kept_preview_button">📄 View Earlier Report</string>

    <!--
      Stopping the run.

      A fourth outcome, and deliberately not one of the three above. The student
      did not fail to get a report - they decided not to wait for one, and the
      three completion screens all describe something that was produced. In
      particular this must never reuse report_generic_title ("Your Report Is
      Incomplete"), which tells a student their answers produced a weak report
      when the truth is they stopped it themselves.

      So a cancelled run has no completion screen at all: it puts the student
      back on the question they submitted from, with every answer still in place,
      and says plainly that nothing was saved. Preview and Continue would both be
      wrong here - there is nothing to preview.
    -->
    <string name="report_cancel_button">Stop and go back</string>
    <string name="report_cancelled_toast">Report generation stopped. Nothing was saved and your answers are still here — submit again whenever you\'re ready.</string>

    <!-- Replaces "This may take 2-3 minutes...". The work regularly runs far
         longer than any fixed estimate, so this promises no duration at all. -->
    <string name="report_generating_hint">⏱️ Please keep this screen open while your report is prepared</string>
